 <section class="section-small about-band" id="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title"><div class="wrap"><div class="section-top"><span class="eyebrow dark">FREQUENT QUESTIONS</span><h2 id="faq-title">Before you start</h2></div><div class="faq-list"><details><summary>Will this website submit a complaint for me?</summary><p>No. It prepares guidance and an editable Word draft only. You must verify the competent authority and submit the final document yourself using an appropriate channel.</p></details><details><summary>Does the free inquiry demo allow me to manage a case?</summary><p>No. It lists main inquiry stages with statutory sections and timelines, including witness and evidence assessment. It does not provide casework, evidence handling, hearings, decision support or reports.</p></details><details><summary>What if my organisation has ten or more workers but I cannot locate an IC?</summary><p>Choose the answer that accurately distinguishes an unconstituted IC from unavailable IC information. The guidance explains what to request and why the proper forum may need confirmation. Do not assume the LC is automatically competent.</p></details><details><summary>Can I request conciliation?</summary><p>Where Section 10 applies, the aggrieved woman may voluntarily request conciliation before the inquiry starts. A monetary settlement cannot form its basis. The free journey includes a separate optional document where its preliminary conditions are met.</p></details><details><summary>Are my selections saved online?</summary><p>This standalone offline preview keeps selections in the page's memory only, and does not have a server-based case store. Do not treat it as a secure repository for real confidential evidence.</p></details><details><summary>Are the paid plans available now?</summary><p>Not through this preview. Their features and prices describe planned offerings. Contact the team for a proposal or readiness information.</p></details></div></div></section>
